<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>01 · UP — 向上、完结体、视线显露与靠近<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.16 & Ch.1 §17</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>UP: Upward, Perfective Completion, Visibility & Approach</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>645</b> 个独立义项 • <b>1935</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 1 (§14, §16–§19) & Chapter 16 (Up, down: Off, out)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>垂直向上路径 (↑) 与「完结体小品词 (Perfective Particle)」</b>：在重力场中，UP 具有绝对垂直方向性（180° 旋转即为 DOWN）。在短语动词中，UP 最核心的贡献是构成<b>完结体短语动词 (Perfective Phrasal Verbs)</b>，表示动作比单独使用动词时更彻底、更完全、更具决定性。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>climb up a tree</i> (透明空间义) → <i>fill up a bag</i> (液面升至容器口 = 完结体) → <i>break up some ice</i> (彻底碎裂) → <i>make up</i> (高习语化) [Table 1.16]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>The very word [chemotherapy] conjures up images of suffering.</i> [Ch.1 §5 COCA]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>Ordinary vs Perfective (Ch.1 §17 & Table 1.16)</b>：普通习语型短语动词（如 <i>make up after a quarrel</i>）透明度低；而完结体短语动词（如 <i>cut up an onion</i> 比 <i>cut</i> 切得更碎，<i>fill up a bag</i> 装满至顶端边缘）具有极高的语义规律性。</li><li><b>显露与接近 (Ch.9 §4.1.3 & Ch.16)</b>：升至视线水平高度（up to eye level）代表变得清晰可见（<i>turn/show up</i>）；水平走近目标直至距离归零代表抵达边界（<i>walk up to sb, catch up with</i>）。</li></ul></div></div></details>

