<details class='sub-section' id='sub_4'><summary class='sub-header'><span><span class='arrow-icon'>▶</span>05 · 水平靠近、赶上齐平、盛装与交出放弃 <span style='font-weight:400;font-size:0.86em;color:#cbd5e1;margin-left:8px;'>Horizontal Approach, Catching up & Capitulation — EPE Ch.16</span></span><span class='sub-meta'>32 义项</span></summary><div class='epe-explain-box'>📖 <b>EPE 认知机制 (Lindstromberg Ch.16)：</b>为什么在平地上走近某人叫 <i>walk/come up to sb</i>？因为站在重要人物或高地前需要“向上走”，更重要的是<b>距离达到零（Up to the target boundary = 抵达目标边界极限）</b>。同理，从落后追赶到与前人齐平叫 <i>catch/keep up with</i>；把双手举高交出武器或把控制权向上交出即为投降放弃（<i>give/yield up</i>）。</div><table><tr><th width='21%'>Phrasal Verb • 语法与语域</th><th width='24%'>🎯 English Definition (WordNet)</th><th width='14%'>🔄 Single-Word Verb</th><th width='41%'>💬 Authentic Examples</th></tr>
<tr data-sep='Separable' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>give <span class='pt-highlight'>up</span></span><span class='sense-badge' title='该短语共有 10 个核心义项'>1/10</span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Separable'>🟢 可拆分 (v. + O + adv.)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：作为正式词 [forfeit] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>lose (s.th.) or lose the right to (s.th.) by some error, offense, or crime</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>forfeit, waive</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span>You've forfeited your right to name your successor.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>②</span>Forfeited property.</div></div></div></td></tr>
<tr data-sep='Separable' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>give <span class='pt-highlight'>up</span></span><span class='sense-badge' title='该短语共有 10 个核心义项'>3/10</span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Separable'>🟢 可拆分 (v. + O + adv.)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：作为正式词 [abandon] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>give up with the intent of never claiming again</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>abandon</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span>Abandon your life to God.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>②</span>She gave up her children to her ex-husband when she moved to Tahiti.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>③</span>We gave the drowning victim up for dead.</div></div></div></td></tr>
<tr data-sep='Separable' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>give <span class='pt-highlight'>up</span></span><span class='sense-badge' title='该短语共有 10 个核心义项'>4/10</span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Separable'>🟢 可拆分 (v. + O + adv.)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：作为正式词 [release] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>part with a possession or right</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>release, relinquish</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span>I am relinquishing my bedroom to the long-term house guest.</div></div>
